~ start
From behind the door a voice can be heard.
Aleksander Asker: ... Alithia. 
alithia: Mister Asker... 
Aleksander Asker: I’ve heard... What you tried to do. 
alithia: ... 
Aleksander Asker: How's your neck? I hope the fish scales are unharmed?
alithia: ... 
Aleksander Asker: You’ve been so lost in thought ever since you came back. It isn’t the first time, mind you, I am starting to think it’s a hobby of yours. 
Aleksander Asker: But I can tell something is weighing your mind even more than you would like to. 
alithia: Hah. Having a personal confessor is a very scary thing. You really can read me like a book, can't you?
Aleksander Asker: Sarcasm won't get you anywhere, Alithia.
alithia: [/shake]Like anything else would?! Like any of these even matter?![shake]
alithia: We are misguided, mislead, deceived even and yet in a very sickening way it never was a lie!!! They never explicitly told us what the truth is!
alithia: And yet we are supposed to preach? Preach what? Empty realities and promises that we don't even understand what they entail?!
Aleksander Asker: ... You’ve always been really meticulous and never let even the smallest of sin escape from you. 
Aleksander Asker: Times you lied as a child. Times your anger overtook you and you broke something. Times when you couldn’t apologise to someone because of your pride. Even times you’ve thought of telling someone something slightly mean. 
alithia: But here I am! I saw everything, but I can't believe everything! What am I supposed to do with myself?! I saw the Divine and I still--
alithia: ...
Aleksander Asker: Alithia...
Aleksander Asker: You’re a bright girl, Alithia. No matter what it is that has happened, I will always be here for you. 
alithia: Even if my selfishness endangers the whole entire Dome?! 
Aleksander Asker: ... 
Aleksander Asker: Just what did you see, Alithia...?
alithia: ... I can't tell you. I am forced onto an implied oath of silence.
Aleksander Asker: ...
Aleksander Asker: What is it that you struggle with then? What is the question burning in your mind?
alithia: ...
alithia: What does it mean for one to be [/shake]divine[shake]?
alithia: Such a stupid question. And yet here is one who grew up with clergy unable to answer it herself.
Aleksander Asker: I see. Hahaha.
alithia: Why are you laughing...?
Aleksander Asker: As much as I praise you at all times and to everyone, you do have one flaw.
Aleksander Asker: You try to comprehend and see the entire future. And not even of just yourself. But of everyone.
Aleksander Asker: Such a foolish task not even a great computer can manage.
alithia: ...!
alithia: ... Then what am I supposed to do?
Aleksander Asker: Alithia. If there is one thing life has taught me, it's this.
Aleksander Asker: To live is to suffer.
alithia: Ugh.
Aleksander Asker: To walk is to feel the weight of every step. To see is to struggle to comprehend what you perceive. To breathe is to move muscles against their own will.
Aleksander Asker: And this goes beyond such small sufferings. You've faced them before. The way life is makes it impossible for us to evade certain feelings.
Aleksander Asker: To lose family to time. To face unacceptance. To see each and every passing moment pass forever, whether sad or happy.
Aleksander Asker: Trying to live a better life comes with even more torment. To train your body, your muscles ache. To study, your brain struggles. To speak, you reveal your flaws.
alithia: Then why...? Why live...? Why did you stop me...? Why didn't you let me end my suffering?
alithia: I don't know. I don't know anything. Everything I do is the wrong actions. And apparently the whole Dome is suffering the consequences.
alithia: Mister Asker. To allow me to live, you also suffer.
Aleksander Asker: Because I love you as my daughter. It's the very same reason that I choose to live. In the same way that me living is causing you to suffer.
alithia: Sniff...
Aleksander Asker: You've always looked at others. You were always able to perceive all that they did. That they said. That they felt.
Aleksander Asker: But that makes it so easy for you to forget. That you are also with us right now.
Aleksander Asker: Alithia. If there is one thing I can guarantee you, is that you will never be alone.
Aleksander Asker: Even if the Dome is about to be destroyed. Even if you would cause the end of the world. Even if you turn into the most despicable human being.
Aleksander Asker: I'll always always love you. And it's when I realised this love, not just for you, but for others as well that I realised.
Aleksander Asker: It is because of love that mankind has continued to live. To suffer.
Aleksander Asker: And it is the very same thing that makes it all worth it. All bareable. And you hold the greatest power I've ever seen. You love the entirety of mankind.
Aleksander Asker: Never mistake love's ache for bad. It is but to make us realise its importance and more importantly, to lend us its strength.
alithia: [/shake]I'm... I'm sorry... I'm sorry, mister Asker...[shake]
Aleksander Asker: Next time you feel the urge, just come to me instead, alright? I cannot truly stop you of course. And I'll always respect your decisions, no matter what they are.
Aleksander Asker: But allow me... To at least try to be there for you.
Alithia starts bawling. It all suddenly flashes by her eyes.
The people she meant along the way. The people she would like to meet.
And them. Prometheus. Enfina. Cyrus...
She doesn't want to just let go. She doesn't want to just go. No matter how much that might hurt her and them...
She wants to live.
After she starts calming down, Aleksander continues.
Aleksander Asker: As for your question... Instead of asking me, I'd like to revert it.
Aleksander Asker: What does it mean for one to be Divine? Is seeing alone truly believing?
alithia: ...!
alithia: Are you possibly implying...?
Aleksander Asker: I'm a believer. I believe that no matter how childish it sounds, It exists. After whoever created the world, created love.
Aleksander Asker: To believe such a being doesn't believe in love, is to not understand the importance and power of it.
Aleksander Asker: I wonder what your answer is going to be. You've always come up with some really sophisticated answer.
alithia: ... Thank you, mister Asker.
Aleksander Asker: I'll be going now. You know how to find me if you need me, don't you?
alithia: Yes. Don't worry. Thank you.
Aleksander Asker: I just want the best for you. And I'll do my everything for you.
alithia: ... I should leave the room too.
=> END